  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Seed Strategy Roundtable</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A comprehensive Seed Strategy Roundtable (3 day event) in Ghana will be organized by the Government of Ghana to review and reform existing seed sector policies and legal frameworks in alignment with the implementation requirements of the GROW24 sub-programme and Feed Ghana Programme. The initiative addresses critical gaps between Ghana&apos;s 2013 National Seed Policy and contemporary agricultural development imperatives, particularly the nation&apos;s transition toward private-sector-led and farmer-cooperative-driven seed systems. The outcomes will include a Ghana Seed Sector Policy Roadmap and a Stakeholder Partnership Framework. The participation of the Netherlands (EKN and private sector) will provide the opportunity to define a potential role for the Netherlands in both the development and implementation of the Roadmap and Partnership framework.</narrative>
  </description>
